.TH KRABBY 1 "August 2026" krabby "User Commands"
.SH NAME
krabby \- an aggressive, performance-obsessed wrapper around cargo
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B krabby
.RI [ args... ]
.br
.B krabby install
.IR crate_or_url...
.RI [ cargo_flags... ]
.br
.B krabby inject
.RI [ profile ]
.IR cmd
.br
.B krabby uninstall
.IR crate
.br
.B krabby update
.br
.B krabby list
.br
.B krabby help
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBkrabby\fR replaces day-to-day \fBcargo build\fR, \fBinstall\fR, and \fBupdate\fR usage with an aggressive build pipeline that auto-tunes build profiles per binary.

It enforces native optimizations (\fB-march=native\fR, \fB-C target-cpu=native\fR), full LTO, \fBlld\fR as the linker, and strict hardening flags (\fBFORTIFY_SOURCE=3\fR, stack protectors, etc.) baked into every build.

On a cache miss, it probes two build profiles per binary (\fBcrosslto\fR and \fBrust\fR) to determine if C/C++ FFI dependencies actually benefit from cross-language LTO. It caches the winning profile locally or globally, and reuses it on future builds to eliminate probing overhead.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B [args...]
Build the local project (auto-detects Cargo.toml). Arguments are passed directly to \fBcargo build\fR. Note: \fB--release\fR and \fB--locked\fR are automatically enabled.
.TP
.B install \fIcrate_or_url...\fR \fI[cargo_flags...]\fR
Install or compile crates from crates.io or Git repositories. Supports multi-binary installs and applies cargo flags sequentially. Note: \fB--locked\fR is automatically enabled.
.TP
.B inject \fI[profile]\fR \fIcmd\fR
Execute an arbitrary command with Krabby's aggressive compiler environment variables injected. The profile defaults to \fBcrosslto\fR but can be explicitly set to \fBrust\fR.
.TP
.B uninstall \fIcrate\fR
Uninstall a cargo crate.
.TP
.B update
Check crates.io and upgrade all installed binaries.
.TP
.B list
List all cargo-installed binaries.
.TP
.B help
Show usage information.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KRABBY_SYNC_ENABLED
Set to 1 to enable pkglist-cargo.txt syncing to ~/dotfiles on install/uninstall.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base directory for the per-binary profile cache. Defaults to ~/.cache.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .v3compile
Drop this file containing just \fBrust\fR or \fBcrosslto\fR in a project's root to skip probing for that project permanently.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/v3compile/<bin_name>
Global cache storing the winning profile for a binary.
.SH NOTES
\fBkrabby\fR binaries are \fBnot portable\fR due to \fB-march=native\fR. They will only run correctly on the CPU they were built on (or a very similar one).
.br
.sp
It leverages \fBRUSTC_BOOTSTRAP=1\fR to enable nightly-gated flags (like \fB-Z build-std\fR) on stable compilers.
.SH SEE ALSO
cargo(1), rustc(1)
